TOO STRONG was the closing claim that the remaining obligation is ONE comparison. Landing it (FiberH0Comparison.lean, fiberRank_gammaTop_eq_fiberH0, hproj-free, sorry-free) showed THREE:
 (a) hbc without h1-vanishing -- not free: A = Z, d = mult-by-2, B = Z/2 refutes it with both terms flat;
 (b) finite-dimensionality of ker d over kappa(t) -- finrank is junk 0 infinite-dimensionally on BOTH sides, and the original's argument against that ran entirely through the hfin I dropped;
 (c) a CARRIER BRIDGE I missed: my Ideal.fiberRank conclusion is NOT the same term as Scheme.Modules.pointRank (rfl fails, different ring and prime), and the only in-tree lemma relating them carries the Flat + Finite binders this drops.

Read 'converts B5's obligation into hbc' as 'converts PART of it'. Detail in I-0949; docstrings corrected in c5f4b684f. Next lane should plan for (a), (b), (c)." 2>&1 | tail -2

